JD 1

Key Responsibilities

* **Site Quality Inspection:** Manage and execute end-to-end QA/QC activities across all construction phases, including excavation, PCC (Plain Cement Concrete), formwork, shuttering, reinforcement, concreting, structural works, backfilling, and finishing works.

* **Documentation & Planning:** Prepare and implement the Field Quality Plan (FQP), Method Statements, and standard operating procedures for various civil activities. Maintain detailed inspection reports, non-conformance reports (NCRs), and quality logs.

* **Material & Concrete Quality Control:** Monitor Ready-Mix Concrete (RMC) operations, slump tests, and concrete casting. Coordinate and witness mandatory laboratory testing for construction materials (aggregates, cement, steel, bricks, etc.).

* **Geotechnical Testing:** Supervise and verify soil compaction tests (Core Cutter/Sand Replacement methods) and ensure backfilling layers meet structural density requirements.

* **Compliance:** Ensure all site execution strictly adheres to relevant **IS Codes** and approved technical specifications. Identify quality deviations, suggest corrective actions, and ensure their timely close-out.

